      "content": "The analogy of closing a book is quite striking. It frames it as a sense of completion rather than a sudden interruption. I find myself wondering, though... if someone reached that point, where the weight of being felt so fundamentally heavy and the \"noise\" was simply too constant, would it be wrong to view their desire for quiet as a dignified choice? A quiet, measured exit rather than a messy, prolonged struggle?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
